cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "WW-DHSVM: Watershed Workflow, retargeted from ATS to DHSVM"
message: >-
  If you use WW-DHSVM in your work, please cite it as below, and please
  also cite Watershed Workflow and DHSVM — this tool is a fork of the
  former and writes inputs for the latter.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-28"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/UConn-EFC/ww-dhsvm/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/UConn-EFC/ww-dhsvm"
url: "https://github.com/UConn-EFC/ww-dhsvm"

authors:
  - given-names: Zhi
    family-names: Li
    email: zhi.2.li@uconn.edu
    affiliation: University of Connecticut
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6240-8971"

abstract: >-
  WW-DHSVM builds complete, runnable cases for the Distributed Hydrology
  Soil Vegetation Model (DHSVM) from a USGS HUC code or a watershed
  polygon. It is a fork of Watershed Workflow v2.1.0 with the ATS
  unstructured-mesh half removed and a DHSVM half added: a regular model
  grid, DHSVM's headerless binary maps, terrain conditioning and D8 flow
  routing confined to the basin, channel delineation with basin-derived
  hydraulic classes, USDA texture and NLCD crosswalks, initial model
  states, the configuration file, and station meteorology from AORC,
  Daymet or NOAA HRRR. Every stage is instrumented with diagnostics and
  figures. The worked example is the entire Connecticut River Basin at
  150 m.

keywords:
  - hydrology
  - DHSVM
  - watershed modeling
  - hydrologic modeling
  - distributed hydrology
  - geospatial
  - Python

